-Foreground (default) returns as soon as the command finishes. To wait a fixed time, run the wait in the foreground; never background a sleep or polling loop. Health-check a background server in a separate call and manage jobs with process_manage. When a command changes directory, trust the result's "cwd" instead of prefixing later commands with cd."""
+Foreground (default) returns as soon as the command finishes. To wait for a background process, call process_manage(action="wait"): it returns the moment the process exits, where a sleep followed by a log read costs a turn per check. A foreground sleep is only for a fixed delay with no process or card behind it; never background a sleep or polling loop. Health-check a background server in a separate call and manage jobs with process_manage. When a command changes directory, trust the result's "cwd" instead of prefixing later commands with cd."""
 
